# ====================
# Documentation (Internal)
# ====================
# Note: `docs/*` (not `docs/`) so git still descends into the directory and the
# negation below can take effect. A directory excluded outright is never walked,
# and any `!` rule for a path inside it is silently ignored.
docs/*
DEVELOPER_GUIDE.md
JOBS_DATASET_SPEC.md
PASS3_PROMPT.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
TASKS.md

# Architecture Decision Records are public — they are the record of why the
# system is shaped the way it is, and must survive the blanket docs/ ignore.
!docs/adr/

# ====================
# Planning & Analysis (Internal)
# ====================
# Working notes and audit reports behind the backlog. Neither these reports
# nor TASKS.md itself are tracked; both are kept local to the working copy.
Plans/

# ====================
# Python
# ====================
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python

# ====================
# Dependencies
# ====================
# All three requirement sets are tracked. requirements-ml.txt and
# requirements-dev.txt were ignored here for a period; CI is a clean clone and
# cannot install what is not in the repository, so the suite could not run and
# "the tests pass" was a claim only reproducible on one machine. They hold
# pinned public package names -- nothing environment-specific, nothing secret.

# ====================
# Virtual Environments
# ====================
.venv/
venv/
ENV/
env/
.virtualenv/

